 confidence"},{"rank":18,"name":"PIPERACILLIN","compound_id":"CHEMBL702","accession":"P37840","score":4.36778,"score_min":-0.924661,"consistent":"no","known_active":false,"moa":"Bacterial penicillin-binding protein inhibitor","note":"fibril; low confidence"},{"rank":19,"name":"PENTETIC ACID","compound_id":"CHEMBL780","accession":"P37840","score":4.30633,"score_min":-0.864956,"consistent":"no","known_active":false,"moa":"Radioactive metals chelating agent","note":"fibril; low confidence"},{"rank":20,"name":"NONOXYNOL 9","compound_id":"CHEMBL1410","accession":"P37840","score":4.29469,"score_min":-0.388844,"consistent":"no","known_active":false,"moa":"Cell membrane disrupting agent","note":"fibril; low confidence"}],"n_screening_hits":0,"top_screening_hits":[],"notes":["Structure is an alpha-synuclein fibril. Top predictions are mostly highly charged molecules binding the fibril surface, and no drug ranks well on all three structures; treat as low confidence."]}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000145335","entrez_id":["6622"],"uniprot":["P37840"],"ncbi_summary":"Alpha-synuclein is a member of the synuclein family, which also includes beta- and gamma-synuclein. Synucleins are abundantly expressed in the brain and alpha- and beta-synuclein inhibit phospholipase D2 selectively. SNCA may serve to integrate presynaptic signaling and membrane trafficking. Defects in SNCA have been implicated in the pathogenesis of Parkinson disease. SNCA peptides are a major component of amyloid plaques in the brains of patients with Alzheimer's disease. Alternatively spliced transcripts encoding different isoforms have been identified for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, Feb 2016].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P37840","text":"Neuronal protein that plays several roles in synaptic activity such as regulation of synaptic vesicle trafficking and subsequent neurotransmitter release (PubMed:20798282, PubMed:26442590, PubMed:28288128, PubMed:30404828). Participates as a monomer in synaptic vesicle exocytosis by enhancing vesicle priming, fusion and dilation of exocytotic fusion pores (PubMed:28288128, PubMed:30404828). Mechanistically, acts by increasing local Ca(2+) release from microdomains which is essential for the enhancement of ATP-induced exocytosis (PubMed:30404828). Also acts as a molecular chaperone in its multimeric membrane-bound state, assisting in the folding of synaptic fusion components called SNAREs (Soluble NSF Attachment Protein REceptors) at presynaptic plasma membrane in conjunction with cysteine string protein-alpha/DNAJC5 (PubMed:20798282). This chaperone activity is important to sustain normal SNARE-complex assembly during aging (PubMed:20798282). Also plays a role in the regulation of the dopamine neurotransmission by associating with the dopamine transporter (DAT1) and thereby modulating its activity (PubMed:26442590)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[{"accession":"P37840","pdb_id":"7wmm","het_id":"1KI","resolution":2.6,"method":"Electron Microscopy","ligand_rule":"SUBJECT_OF_INVESTIGATION","datasets":["Mathys et al. 2019"],"ligand_name":"2-bromanyl-4-[(~{E})-2-[6-[2-(2-fluoranylethoxy)ethyl-methyl-amino]-5-methyl-1,3-benzothiazol-2-yl]ethenyl]phenol","ligand_class":"drug-like or studied compound","ligand_note":null,"entry_title":"alpha-synuclein fibril-F0502B complex","first_author":"Tao, Y.Q.","n_authors":4,"journal":"To Be Published","year":null,"doi":null,"citation_url":null},{"accession":"P37840","pdb_id":"7ynf","het_id":"V79","resolution":2.5,"method":"Electron Microscopy","ligand_rule":"SUBJECT_OF_INVESTIGATION","datasets":["Mathys et al. 2019"],"ligand_name":"copper;trisodium;18-(2-carboxylatoethyl)-20-(carboxylatomethyl)-12-ethenyl-7-ethyl-3,8,13,17-tetramethyl-17,18-dihydroporphyrin-21,23-diide-2-carboxylate","ligand_class":"drug-like or studied compound","ligand_note":"a copper chl